<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jan van Riebeeck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1619">1619</a>–<a href="/years/1677">1677</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jan van Riebeeck was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> official who landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/table-bay">Table Bay</a> in 1652 to set up a station supplying fresh food to ships sailing to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">East Indies</a>, the beginning of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a>. He commanded the Cape until 1662, when he became governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> until 1665. He later served as secretary of the Company's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-the-indies">Council of the Indies</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jan-van-riebeeck.jpg" alt="Jan van Riebeeck" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_van_Jan_van_Riebeeck_(1619-77)._Bevelhebber_van_Kaap_de_Goede_Hoop_en_van_Malacca_en_secretaris_van_de_Hoge_Regering_van_Batavia,_SK-A-805.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
